htrflow's reading-order fix, carried here until AI-Riksarkivet/htrflow has it.

Commit 7c586a7a8b8a2bb124e28deea825a1fd18e104ef "Fix reading order quirk"
(2026-10-20) in htrflow's Azure Repos main; not on GitHub's main, which the
image builds from. get_region_location tested the left and right margins
before the top and bottom ones, so a region above the print space at its
edge was read as a side margin and ReadingOrderMarginalia put it after the
body text. The image build applies this to HTRFLOW_REF with `git apply`,
which refuses it if it no longer matches; remove this file and the
htrflow-patched stage when HTRFLOW_REF has the commit.

diff --git a/src/htrflow/utils/layout.py b/src/htrflow/utils/layout.py
index 11586b2..2240cfa 100644
--- a/src/htrflow/utils/layout.py
+++ b/src/htrflow/utils/layout.py
@@ -167,12 +167,12 @@ def get_region_location(printspace: Bbox, region: Bbox) -> RegionLocation:
     overlap = printspace.intersection(region)
     if overlap is not None and region.area > 0 and (overlap.area / region.area) > 0.5:
         return RegionLocation.PRINTSPACE
-    if region.xmax >= printspace.xmax:
-        return RegionLocation.MARGIN_RIGHT
-    if region.xmin <= printspace.xmin:
-        return RegionLocation.MARGIN_LEFT
     if region.ymin <= printspace.ymin:
         return RegionLocation.MARGIN_TOP
     if region.ymax >= printspace.ymax:
         return RegionLocation.MARGIN_BOTTOM
+    if region.xmax >= printspace.xmax:
+        return RegionLocation.MARGIN_RIGHT
+    if region.xmin <= printspace.xmin:
+        return RegionLocation.MARGIN_LEFT
     return RegionLocation.PRINTSPACE
